{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "9a36f766-f3cc-8a69-b77e-dd99288c1fbc",
  "created_at": "2026-02-04T10:42:07-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Lucille Grasso",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:39:41-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Denise. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:39:45-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, Denise. Yes, hello. Um, my name is Lucille Grasso. I am calling because the truck, the trash truck, it broke my bin this morning."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:39:55-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, I'm sorry about that. Which bin is it, the trash or the recycling?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:01-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The recycling one. The blue one. [pause] Excuse me, I am cutting onions, so I am sniffling. Do not worry, I am not sick."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:10-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No worries at all. Onions will do it. So the blue bin. What happened to it, exactly?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:17-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The lid, it is, how do you say, torn off. And one side is cracked, a big crack. The man, he lift it with the machine and then he drop it hard on the street. I saw from the window."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:32-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so the lid's gone and the side is cracked. That's definitely worth replacing. Can I get the address where it's picked up?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:41-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. It is four fifty-five Ayrault Street. [pause] Four, five, five."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:46-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four fifty-five Ayrault, got it. That's up on the Hill, right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:51-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, yes, Historic Hill. Sorry, one moment. [pause] The onions, they are strong today."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:57-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Take your time, Lucille."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:40:59-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. So, how do I ask for a new one? Is there a form, or I should come to the office? I do not know how it works."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:41:10-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No need to come in. I can put in the replacement request for you right now over the phone. I'll note that it was damaged by the truck during pickup, so it should be a straight swap."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:41:24-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Oh, that is very good. Thank you, you are very kind."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:41:29-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Do you want it left at the same spot, by the curb?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:41:34-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, by the curb, next to the gate. The broken one, I leave it there too?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:41:40-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, leave the broken one out. They'll take it when they drop the new one. Should be within a week or so. Can I have a number in case they need to reach you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:41:53-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. It is four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-eight-nine."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:41:56-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-eight-nine. Perfect, that's all in."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:41:59-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you, Denise. God bless you. I go back to my onions now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-04T10:42:04-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Enjoy your cooking. Take care, Lucille."
    }
  ],
